// Temperate fish, frogs, snakes and the honey bee (Appendix B tier 1), Palearctic and
// Nearctic: simulated as numbers per ecological cell. Fish densities are per km² of their
// water, a colony species' (the honey bee's) are colonies per km². "litter" is the eggs a
// female lays (fish, frogs), the young born alive (snakes) or the swarms a colony sends out.
// Values rounded from general references (Kottelat & Freyhof's Handbook of European
// Freshwater Fishes, herpetological atlases, Seeley's The Lives of Bees).
